# Chemistry & Chemical Engineering Taste Considerations & Philosophical Probes
#
# Aesthetic dialectics, scale transitions, environmental ethics, and wonder probes across the chemical sciences.

#>spw_cache_univ_chem_cheme_taste
#:cache #!chemistry_and_chemical_engineering
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Articulate the aesthetic tensions, epistemological differences, and ethical commitments bridging pure molecular chemistry and macroscopic chemical process engineering."
  ~#resonance: "Molecular choreography, scale-up physics, industrial stewardship, and the sublime symmetry of transport phenomena"
}

^["the_dialectic_of_flask_and_pipe"]{
  cultural_contrast: "The pure chemist and the chemical engineer look at the same reaction through radically different epistemological lenses."
  distinctions: #[
    "Milligram purity vs. Metric ton continuity: The chemist celebrates a pristine 50 mg crystal in an NMR tube; the engineer asks how to produce 5,000 tons per year without overheating the reactor",
    "Equilibrium thermodynamics vs. Transport limits: The chemist focuses on Gibbs free energy minimization; the engineer knows that reaction velocity is almost always governed by mass transfer across turbulent film boundaries",
    "Batch isolation vs. Recycle networks: The chemist throws away spent solvents after a wash; the engineer designs closed-loop solvent recovery units to achieve 99.8% material circularity"
  ]
}

^["the_aesthetics_of_molecular_choreography"]{
  molecular_sublime: "A catalytic cycle is a choreographed ballet performed by billions of molecules at trillions of revolutions per second."
  aesthetic_elements: #[
    "Orbital Symmetry: The breathtaking mathematical inevitability of Woodward-Hoffmann rules, where the phase of a wavefunction dictates whether four atoms must twist conrotatory or disrotatory",
    "Chiral Handedness: The poetic asymmetry of nature, where swapping two substituents on a single tetrahedral carbon shifts the scent from spearmint to caraway",
    "Catalytic Turnover: The magic of a single rhodium atom coordinating, activating, and releasing ten thousand substrate molecules without ever suffering fatigue"
  ]
}

^["the_ethics_of_industrial_scale"]{
  grave_responsibility: "When chemistry leaves the bench and enters the refinery, a minor calculation error can alter the chemistry of the planet's atmosphere or devastate a watershed."
  ethical_imperatives: #[
    "The Shadow of Disaster: Remembering Bhopal, Texas City, and Flixborough; realizing that process safety is a sacred moral duty, not a bureaucratic checklist",
    "Persistent Molecules (PFAS & Plastics): Designing synthetic pathways with ultimate circular degradation in mind, refusing to create persistent chemical curses",
    "Decarbonization at the Root: Re-engineering the Haber-Bosch ammonia process and Portland cement calcination—the two pillars of modern human survival and massive fossil emissions"
  ]
}

^"taste"{
  ~#taste: "To study chemistry is to witness the alphabet of the universe; to study chemical engineering is to write novels with that alphabet in the physical world."
  ~#wonder: "Can human society reinvent its entire chemical manufacturing foundation—replacing fossil petrochemistry with electro-catalytic, bio-derived feedstocks—within a single generation?"
}

^"invariants"{
  "Chemical synthesis must prioritize green chemistry principles (atom economy, safer solvents, energy efficiency) alongside chemical yield.",
  "Scale-up of any exothermic chemical process requires rigorous heat transfer modeling before physical pilot-scale ignition.",
  "Engineers and chemists share collective ethical accountability for the complete lifecycle fate of synthesized compounds.",
}

#>wonder_chem_cheme_taste_1
?["Can electro-catalytic nitrogen reduction ever match the volumetric energy efficiency of the Haber-Bosch process at ambient temperatures?"]{
  #:depth #!philosophical ~#lens(thermodynamic_limits)
  ~#hypothesis: "Ambient electrochemical nitrogen fixation will overcome the kinetic inertness of the N≡N triple bond only when biomimetic multi-electron relay clusters (mimicking nitrogenase FeMo-co) are coupled to gas-diffusion electrodes, replacing 200-bar Haber-Bosch plants with distributed modular farm-scale reactors."
  !probe{ "Measure Faradaic efficiency, ammonia production rate (umol/cm2/hr), and energy consumption per kg-NH3 in transition-metal cluster gas-diffusion cells vs Haber-Bosch benchmarks." }
  $%[electrocatalysis.faradaic_efficiency_percent, energetics.kwh_per_kg_ammonia]
}

#>wonder_chem_cheme_taste_2
?["What psychological threshold shifts a student's intuition from treating matter as static objects to experiencing matter as dynamic fields of electron probability?"]{
  #:depth #!cognitive ~#lens(epistemic_transformation)
  ~#hypothesis: "The ontological shift occurs during physical chemistry when a student solves the Schrödinger equation for the hydrogen atom and realizes that the solid 'table' before them is 99.9999999% empty space held rigid solely by Pauli exclusion and electrostatic force."
  !probe{ "Conduct longitudinal cognitive interviews with chemistry and chemical engineering majors across their four-year sequence tracking semantic descriptions of molecular matter." }
  $%[cognitive.matter_ontology_index, pedagogy.conceptual_quantum_shift]
}
